title: Dungeons
intro: Floors of rooms and corridors made from a seed, with the player, the stairs and the monsters put in place. No code.
project: Empty | Deep Halls

chapter: A dungeon | Entity > Genres > Dungeons > Dungeon
select: Main Camera
set: Camera.Size = 17
deselect
create: Dungeon
explain: component:DungeonGenerator | Dungeon Generator | A Dungeon Generator on a tilemap fills it with a dungeon: rooms of different sizes, joined by corridors, cut out of solid wall.
explain: field:DungeonGenerator.Rooms | Rooms | It makes up to this many rooms, between the smallest and biggest room sizes, and a couple of extra corridors so there's more than one way round.
explain: field:DungeonGenerator.Seed | Seed | The seed picks the dungeon. Zero makes a new one every game.
menu: Entity > Generate Dungeon
wait: 0.8
menu: Entity > Generate Dungeon
wait: 0.8
say: Generate Dungeon shows one in the editor. With a seed of zero, it's a different dungeon every time.
set: DungeonGenerator.Seed = 140
menu: Entity > Generate Dungeon
expecttile: Dungeon 28, 14 = -1
expecttile: Dungeon 0, 0 = 0
say: The same seed always makes the same dungeon, so this is the one the game will play.

chapter: Who goes where | Players, the exit and spawns
deselect
create: Grid Player
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Stairs
set: Sprite.Tint = #F2C94C
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Slime
set: Sprite.Tint = #57AB5A
set: Sprite.Size = 0.7, 0.7
menu: Entity > Save as Prefab
menu: Entity > Delete
say: A grid player, some stairs, and a slime saved as a prefab.
select: Dungeon
explain: field:DungeonGenerator.Players | Players | The entity called Player goes in the middle of the first room.
pick: DungeonGenerator.Exit = Stairs
explain: field:DungeonGenerator.Exit | Exit | The stairs go in the room the longest walk away. Stepping onto them goes down to the next floor.
choose: DungeonGenerator.Spawns:add = Slime
editorset: DungeonGenerator.Spawns:most:1 = 6
editorset: DungeonGenerator.Spawns:least:1 = 6
expectvalue: Dungeon.DungeonGenerator.Spawns = Slime 6
explain: field:DungeonGenerator.Spawns | Spawns | Pick a prefab to add it, then how many: six slimes, scattered through the other rooms. A row can be a range too, like one to three potions.
menu: Entity > Generate Dungeon
expectat: Player = 4.5, 1.5
expectat: Stairs = -20.5, -7.5
say: Generating again puts the player and the stairs in place, as one undo step.

chapter: Down the stairs | Play it
play
wait: 0.5
expectcount: Slime = 6
explain: game | Spawns | As the game starts, the six slimes appear in the rooms. They never land in the player's room, on the stairs, or on each other.
hold: Left 4.2
expectat: Player = -20.5, 1.5
say: The player walks the corridor, and the walls stop it.
hold: Down 1.6
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Dungeon.DungeonGenerator.Floor = 2
expectcount: Slime = 6
explain: game | Floor two | Onto the stairs, and it's the next floor: a new dungeon, new slimes, and the player in its first room. Each floor sends a Floor message for a counter to show.
stop
say: That's a dungeon generator with no code. The tiles and the floor are saved with the scene, so a rewind goes back to the floor you were on.
